The same third-party report as third-party-sogou-uaf.log, but from a build that
does NOT replace global operator delete -- the stock MSVC ASan thunk is frame
#0 of the free stack and there is no gyFree in between.

Kept as a separate case so the allocator-plumbing skip is proved to work in
both worlds: the day tests\framework\Test.cpp stops overriding the global
operator, or somebody points this classifier at a log from a different binary,
the answer must not change.

SECOND JOB, AND DO NOT "FIX" IT: the suite summary line below is encoded in
GBK, while every other fixture here has it in UTF-8.  That is deliberate.  The
integrity sentinel in classify-asan.ps1 must match the SHAPE of that line, not
its bytes -- the suite is compiled /utf-8 today, but the day somebody drops
that flag the same words reach the log as GBK, and a sentinel that had been
pinned to UTF-8 bytes would fail the gate on every run for no reason.  One
fixture in the other encoding is what keeps that claim honest.  If you
normalise this file's encoding, the sentinel is untested in that direction.
